      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem will be occured when getActiveSessions is called many times.\nPlease imagine below situation.\n- calling state, then \"com.android.server.telecom session\" is active.\nand the session is global priority session\n- When getActiveSessions is called, the session is added to\nmCachedActiveLists of MediaSessionStack\n\n- And that causes some problem with onActiveSessionsChanged\n\nI made test application like below.\n-----------------\nMediaSessionManager msm \u003d (MediaSessionManager) getSystemService(Context.MEDIA_SESSION_SERVICE);\nmsm.addOnActiveSessionsChangedListener(new MediaSessionManager.OnActiveSessionsChangedListener() {\n    @Override\n    public void onActiveSessionsChanged(@Nullable List\u003cMediaController\u003e list) {\n        Log.e(\"hmhm\", \"hmhm active session size : \" + list.size());\n    }\n}, null, null);\n-----------------\n\nCall start and stop many times. And result is next.\n...\n09-29 00:59:49.064 5247-5247/sec.com.mediasessiontest E/hmhm: hmhm size : 21\n09-29 00:59:50.574 5247-5247/sec.com.mediasessiontest E/hmhm: hmhm size : 22\n09-29 00:59:51.420 5247-5247/sec.com.mediasessiontest E/hmhm: hmhm size : 23\n09-29 00:59:54.386 5247-5247/sec.com.mediasessiontest E/hmhm: hmhm size : 24\n\nbecause com.android.server.telecom session is added duplicates",
