      "writtenOn": "2017-09-29T08:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- calling state, then \"com.android.server.telecom session\" is active.\n- and the session is global priority session\n\nMake session global priority after the session becomes active is the problem here.\nGlobal priority session should be in the MediaSessionService instead of the MediaSessionStack, so it shouldn\u0027t be cached in the mCachedActiveLists.\n\nIf you only remove duplicated global priority session because of the misuse, the session will be at the MediaSessionStack and MediaSessionService.mGlobalPrioritySession would remain null.\n\n\nThe proper fix for your case would be one of the followings.\n1. Make a session global priority before it becomes active.\n2. Move a session from the MediaSessionStack to the MediaSessionService when the session becomes the global priority.\nPick one of the approach depending on your case. I can review your CL for either approach, but I prefer the first one because that\u0027s the same as our implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "d631971a_16913d72",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 226,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 226,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "dde74f3c411600228d48633378f8076fbaa5c357",
